<title>USA: U.S. Stockpile sells surplus bismuth.</title>
<headline>U.S. Stockpile sells surplus bismuth.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-09-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. Defense National Stockpile Center said Tuesday it sold 185,448 pounds of surplus bismuth to MCP Metalspecialties Inc of Fairfield, Connecticut, for an approximate current market value of $580,000.</p>
<p>The long-term sale completes the fiscal 1996 offers of bismuth. The first fiscal 1997 sale is scheduled for October 23, the agency said.</p>
<p>-- Washington Commodities Desk (202) 898-8489</p>
</text>
